==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{der|is|non|heimskr||foolish, silly; who has never been from home}}, from {{m|is|heima||home}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|eimskʏr|lang=is}}

===Adjective===
{{is-adj|heimskari|heimskastur}}

# [[stupid]], [[foolish]], [[dumb]]
#: ''Ógn er hann '''heimskur'''.''
#:: Oh how very '''stupid''' he is.
#: ''Að gera einhvern '''heimskan'''.'' (''synonym:'' {{m|is|forheimska}})
#:: To '''stultify''' someone.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|heimskt er heimaalið barn}} (travel broadens the mind; homish is the home-bred bairn)

====Related terms====
* {{l|is|heimska}}
* {{l|is|Heimski}} (a nickname; compare the cognomen {{m|is|Brutus}}, from {{m|la|brūtus||heavy, unwieldy; dull, stupid}})

